{"format":1,"key":"zone:durotar","path":"/lore/zone/durotar","name":"Durotar","kind":"zone","label":"Zone","zone":{"key":"durotar","name":"Durotar","path":"/lore/zone/durotar"},"levels":"Levels 1-10","description":"In Durotar's red canyons, young orcs and Darkspear trolls prove themselves to the New Horde. Warchief Thrall founded this arid homeland after the Third…","intro":[],"clips":[{"id":"zone:durotar","part":"narration","anchor":"story","title":"The story","paras":["In Durotar's red canyons, young orcs and Darkspear trolls prove themselves to the New Horde. Warchief Thrall founded this arid homeland after the Third War and named it for his father, Durotan. The Southfury River and the Great Sea hem it in. Razor Hill and the warrior city of Orgrimmar rise from its rock, while quilboar tribes and stranded Alliance troops still hold out.","When Thrall led his people across the Great Sea to Kalimdor, he chose an untamed frontier on purpose. Here the orcs would earn an honest living through labor and grit, not conquest. The cracked red soil, baked gullies and towering spires remind them of Draenor before its destruction. Water is scarce and little of the land can be farmed, but the Horde embraced its natural defenses and stark grandeur. Across the Southfury to the west lie the open Barrens, and to the north the ruined wilds of Azshara. Durotar is proof that the orcs have forged their own destiny.","The Horde holds Durotar, but keeping it is still a war. Razormane quilboar, pushed out when the nation was founded, raid farms and settlements from the western crags. In the south, what is left of Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's Kul Tiras fleet still holds the crumbling garrison of Tiragarde Keep under Lieutenant Benedict, and refuses to surrender. Worse, the demonic Burning Blade coven lurks in hidden ravines and deep sea caves, tempting young orcs back to fel power.","On the southern coast, Sen'jin Village is the staging ground of the exiled Darkspear trolls, led by Master Gadrin. They lost their home on the nearby Echo Isles when the witch doctor Zalazane lost his mind and used dark voodoo to enslave his own kin. Unable to take the islands back alone, the Darkspear count on new orc and troll warriors from the Valley of Trials to break Zalazane's hold and secure the coast."],"hash":"020a34","voices":{"male-narrator":{"sha":"891a552c70","sec":111},"female-narrator":{"sha":"de7c28933b","sec":118}}}],"sources":[{"kind":"wiki","title":"Durotar (Classic)","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Durotar_(Classic)"},{"kind":"wiki","title":"Durotar","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Durotar"}],"related":[{"p":"/lore/zone/orgrimmar","n":"Orgrimmar","k":"zone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/valley-of-trials","n":"Valley of Trials","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/razor-hill","n":"Razor Hill","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/sen-jin-village","n":"Sen'jin Village","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/echo-isles","n":"Echo Isles","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/tiragarde-keep","n":"Tiragarde Keep","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/zone/barrens","n":"The Barrens","k":"zone"},{"p":"/lore/zone/ragefire","n":"Ragefire Chasm","k":"dungeon"},{"p":"/lore/item/shimmerweed","n":"Shimmerweed","k":"item"},{"p":"/lore/quest/503-goldir","n":"Gol'dir","k":"quest"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/bladefist-bay","n":"Bladefist Bay","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/burning-blade-coven","n":"Burning Blade Coven","k":"subzone"}],"children":[{"p":"/lore/subzone/bladefist-bay","n":"Bladefist Bay","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/burning-blade-coven","n":"Burning Blade Coven","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/darkspear-strand","n":"Darkspear Strand","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/deadeye-shore","n":"Deadeye Shore","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/drygulch-ravine","n":"Drygulch Ravine","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/dustwind-cave","n":"Dustwind Cave","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/echo-isles","n":"Echo Isles","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/hidden-path","n":"Hidden P